-- title:
--   Closed boxes and box-supported functions on the plane
-- statement:
--   For $M\ge0$:
--
--   1. **Closed box.** $\mathrm{closedBox}(M)=[-M,M]\times[-M,M]\subset\mathbb R^2$.
--   2. **Box support.** A function $f$ on the plane with values in a type with zero is supported in the box of radius $M$ if
--   $$
--   f(z)\ne0\implies|z_1|\le M\ \text{and}\ |z_2|\le M .
--   $$
--
--   Approximation arguments first treat continuous functions supported in a box. There the sampled grid matrices are finite and converge, and the general $L^3$ case then follows by density.
-- source:
